%N A038747 Number of equivalence classes under rotations and reflections of n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice having exactly 1 pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A038747 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n), the n-th term of this sequence is p_{n,m}^{(l)} with m=1 and l=2. These numbers are given in Table II (p. 1093) in the paper. This sequence can be used for the calculation of sequence A033155(n) via Eq. (5) in the paper by Nemirovsky et al. (1992). (Note that, by equations (7b) in the paper, p_{n,1}^{(1)} = 0 for all n >= 1.) - _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 03 2019
%C A038747 In Table B1 (pp. 4738-4739) of the published version of Bennett-Wood et al. (1998), corresponding to Table 4 (pp. 26-28) in Appendix B of the arXiv version, the authors tabulated c_n(k)/4, for various values of n and k, where c_n(k) is the number of SAWs of length n with k nearest-neighbor contacts. Here, the letter k stands for the letter m in the previous paragraph. Bennett-Wood et al. (1998) worked only with a square lattice (i.e., d=2), unlike Nemirovsky et al. (1992), who worked with a d-dimensional hypercubic lattice. Both papers deal with SAWs = self-avoiding walks. We have c_n(1) = A033155(n) = 8*p_{n,1}^{(2)}, so a(n) = p_{n,1}^{(2)} = (c_n(1)/4)/2. Thus the values tabulated for k=1 must be divided by 2 to obtain terms of the current sequence. - _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 05 2019 [Clarified by _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026]
%C A038747 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026: (Start)
%C A038747 Previous name was: Coefficients arising in the enumeration of configurations of linear chains.
%C A038747 Rotations and reflections act on the ordered vertex sequence; reversal is not included, so the start and end remain distinguished.
%C A038747 (End)
%H A038747 D. Bennett-Wood, I. G. Enting, D. S. Gaunt, A. J. Guttmann, J. L. Leask, A. L. Owczarek, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1088/0305-4470/31/20/010">Exact enumeration study of free energies of interacting polygons and walks in two dimensions</a>, J. Phys. A: Math. Gen. 31 (1998), 4725-4741.
%H A038747 D. Bennett-Wood, I. G. Enting, D. S. Gaunt, A. J. Guttmann, J. L. Leask, A. L. Owczarek, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9803359">Exact enumeration study of free energies of interacting polygons and walks in two dimensions</a>, arXiv:cond-mat/9803359 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 1998.
%H A038747 M. E. Fisher and B. J. Hiley, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1731729">Configuration and free energy of a polymer molecule with solvent interaction</a>, J. Chem. Phys., 34 (1961), 1253-1267.
%H A038747 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090) and Eq. 7b (p. 1093).
%F A038747 a(n) = A033155(n)/8 for n >= 1. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026
%e A038747 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 09 2026: (Start)
%e A038747 a(1) = a(2) = 0 because a self-avoiding walk with fewer than 3 steps cannot have a pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%e A038747 a(3) = 1. The eight 3-step walks counted by A033155(3) = 8 form one equivalence class under rotations and reflections, represented by
%e A038747   o---o
%e A038747   |   |
%e A038747   S...X
%e A038747 Here S marks the start, X the end, and the dotted segment the unique contact; the dotted segment is not a step of the walk.
%e A038747 (End)
%Y A038747 Cf. A033155 (corresponding rooted square-lattice walks), A038746 (companion coefficient for m=0), A038749 (companion coefficient for l=3), A047057 (corresponding rooted cubic-lattice walks).
%K A038747 nonn,walk,more,changed
%O A038747 1,4
%A A038747 _N. J. A. Sloane_, May 02 2000
